+// AI(W906-MEMO) 20260927: the memo stand-ins now REALLY store lines (user 0927 07:2x: memory growth "由你建議方式修改",
+//   disk logs "忠於翻譯").  The note above is history: it asked for exactly this, with assertions (tests/test_memo_log.cpp).
+//   - Add / Count / Clear / SaveToFile behave like golden TMemo->Lines: one item per Add; SaveToFile writes every line
+//     + CRLF, raw bytes, no BOM -- the same as vclcompat TStringList::SaveToFile (TStringList.cpp:262-267).  A failed
+//     open returns silently; golden VCL raises EFCreateError there (DEVIATION, same as vclcompat's TStringList).
+//   - Defensive memory cap (DEVIATION, only for paths golden never bounds): past kLineCap lines the OLDEST are dropped.
+//     4096 is above every golden threshold on these memos (census 0927: meShuttle1/2 >2048 in AddShuttleMessage and
+//     >1024 in acarry / OutShuttleLog, memoAutoClean >2048 save-then-clear, mmE84Log >=500, mmTesterLog cleared with
+//     mmTCPIPCommLog >2000), so it never fires before golden's own clear or save and never truncates the 2049-line csv.
